  "notes": "SYNTHETIC HDR COMPOSITE OF REGISTERED VIRTUAL EXPOSURES, NOT A SINGLE DETECTOR FRAME. Same scene and telescope as the single exposure, recorded as a ladder of six frames whose effective exposure t × 10^−ND steps by ~10³ (the sensor's own dynamic range): 20 µs and 20 ms through ND 6, then 20 µs, 20 ms, 2 s and 120 s unfiltered. The short frames record the disk and photon ring, the long ones the stars and sky. The frames are merged in linear units (saturated frames dropped per pixel, dark subtracted, maximum-likelihood rate) and shown with one global curve that removes the empty range of intensities between the brightest star and the faintest disk pixel. Optics are ideal (Airy core plus 2″ blur, no scattered-light halo); a real telescope would show glare around a source this bright.",
